{"name":"Cake Dough","hex":"#fce0a8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rich, sweet dessert food, typically made of flour, sugar, and eggs and baked in an oven, and often covered in icing.","A small mass of baked dough, especially a thin loaf from unleavened dough."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Coat (something) with a crust of solid material.","To form into a cake, or mass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cake"},{"term":"dough","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick, malleable substance made by mixing flour with other ingredients such as water, eggs, or butter, that is made into a particular form and then baked.","Money."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make into dough."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dough"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cake","blocks":[{"text":"Cake is a baker's confectionery made by combining flour with a liquid, a fat or both, and usually with a leavening agent. Cakes are usually baked, but can be griddled. In their oldest forms, cakes were modifications of bread, but cakes now cover a wide range of preparations that can be simple or elaborate and which share features with other desserts such as pastries, meringues, custards, and pies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Pound_layer_cake.jpg/330px-Pound_layer_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cake","wikidata":"Q13276"},{"title":"Dough","blocks":[{"text":"Dough is a malleable, sometimes elastic paste most commonly made from flour or meal. Dough is typically made by mixing flour with a small amount of water or other liquid, and sometimes includes yeast, other leavening agents, or ingredients such as fats or flavourings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Dough.jpg/330px-Dough.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&u